        "7": {
          "id": "7",
          "name": "gamelab-intro.html",
          "contents": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html>\n  <head>\n    <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"style.css\">\n  </head>\n  <body>\n\n    <!-- link back to the main page -->\n    <a class=\"back-link\" href=\"index.html\">Back to Discovering Video Game Development</a>\n\n    <!-- Title -->\n    <h1>Game Lab: Code Your Own Animations and Games</h1>\n\n    <!-- hero image -->\n    <div class=\"page-image\">\n      <img src=\"game-lab.png\" alt=\"Illustrated characters from Code.org's Game Lab, including a zebra, a bunny, and a crab\">\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- informational paragraphs -->\n    <p>Game Lab is a programming environment from Code.org where you can build animations and simple games featuring characters, called sprites, that move and interact with each other. It's designed for beginners, so you don't need any prior coding experience to get started.</p>\n\n    <p>In Game Lab, you write your program in JavaScript, either by typing code directly or by snapping together drag-and-drop blocks. You can draw shapes, add sprites, control how they move and respond to input like keyboard presses or mouse clicks, and bring a whole scene to life with just a few lines of code.</p>\n\n    <p>Many students use Game Lab to build on skills they've already picked up from other units, like using variables, loops, and functions, and apply them to something visual and interactive. Once your project is working, you can share it with a link in just a few seconds.</p>\n\n    <p>Curious to try it yourself? Code.org's Game Lab curriculum walks you through everything from your first shape on the screen to building a complete, playable game.</p>\n\n    <!-- image citation -->\n    <div class=\"citation\">\n      <p>Image from Code.org's Game Lab curriculum</p>\n    </div>\n\n  </body>\n</html>\n",
          "folderId": "0",
          "active": false
        },
        "8": {
          "id": "8",
          "name": "index.html",
          "contents": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html>\n  <head>\n    <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"style.css\">\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    \n    <!-- Title -->\n    <h1>Discovering Video Game Development</h1>\n    \n    <!-- informational paragraph -->\n    <p>Ever wondered how video games are made? Behind every game is a team of creative minds working together, from the first sketch to the final level. Video game development combines art, storytelling, programming, and sound design to create immersive worlds for players to explore.</p> \n    \n    <!-- images -->\n    <div class=\"container1\">\n      <img src=\"world-design.png\" alt=\"world design\">\n      <img src=\"character-design.png\" alt=\"character design\">\n      <img src=\"enemy-design.png\" alt=\"enemy design\">\n    </div>\n    \n    <!-- info -->\n    <p>Video games start as ideas that grow into stories and worlds, thanks to the talent of designers, artists, and programmers. Every character, quest, and puzzle is carefully crafted to bring joy and challenge to gamers worldwide.</p>\n    \n    <!-- images -->\n    <div class=\"container2\">\n      <img src=\"code.png\" alt=\"game code\">\n      <p>It's a journey from concept to coding, with artists bringing characters to life and programmers solving complex problems to make the game run smoothly.</p>\n    </div>\n    \n    <h2>Learn More:</h2>\n    <p>Curious about how to get started in game development? <a href=\"gamelab-intro.html\">Explore more about creating your own game with Code.org</a>.</p>\n    \n    <!-- image citation -->\n    <div class=\"citation\">\n      <p>All images created by chatGPT</p>\n    </div>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  </body>\n</html>",
          "folderId": "0",
          "active": false
        },
        "9": {
          "id": "9",
          "name": "style.css",
          "contents": "/* 1) ADD A RULE SET FOR EACH PSEUDO-CLASS TO STYLE THE ANCHOR TAG */\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n/* body style */\nbody {\n  background-color: #f3eff6;\n  text-align: center;\n  font-family: Arial;\n}\n\n/* title style */\nh1 {\n  font-family: Arial;\n  font-size: 36px;\n  text-align: center;\n}\n\nh2 {\n  font-size: 24px;\n}\n\n/* paragraph style */\np {\n  font-size: 18px;\n}\n\n/* image flex layout style */\n.container1 {\n  display: flex;\n  flex-direction: row;\n  justify-content: space-around;\n  align-items: center;\n}\n\n/* image flex layout style */\n.container2 {\n  display: flex;\n  flex-direction: row;\n  align-items: center;\n  justify-content: center;\n}\n\n/* image style */\nimg {\n  border-style: solid;\n  border-radius: 15px;\n  width: 350px;\n  margin: 15px;\n}\n\n/* citation style */\n.citation {\n  height: 300px;\n  display: flex;\n  justify-content: center;\n  align-items: flex-end;\n}\n\n.citation > p {\n  font-size: 12px;\n  font-style: italic;\n}\n\n/* styles for the new gamelab-intro.html page */\n.back-link {\n  margin: 15px;\n  font-family: Arial;\n  font-size: 16px;\n  color: orchid;\n  text-decoration: none;\n}\n\n.back-link:hover {\n  text-decoration: underline;\n}\n\n.page-image {\n  display: flex;\n  justify-content: center;\n}\n\n.page-image img {\n  width: 400px;\n}",
          "folderId": "0",
          "active": true
        },
